   {
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
     {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Direct Hair Implantation completely scarless compared to traditional FUE?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
       "@type": "Answer",
       "text": "No. This is a common misconception. Both techniques usually involve FUE-style extraction from the donor area. That means tiny punch sites are created to remove grafts. These marks are very small. They usually heal well. But no surgical extraction is truly “scarless.” Direct Hair Implantation mainly changes the implantation method. It does not eliminate the extraction sites. So, it is better to say both methods are minimally invasive. Not completely scarless."
      }
     },
     {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why do some clinics charge significantly more for DHI or implanter pen surgeries in Bangalore?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
       "@type": "Answer",
       "text": "There are a few reasons. Implanter pen surgery may require special instruments. It may also need more loading assistance and more procedural time. The workflow can be more demanding. However, higher cost does not always mean better results. Some clinics use the term “DHI” as a premium marketing label. Patients should ask what exactly is included. Ask these questions: Who will extract the grafts? Who will implant the grafts? How many grafts are planned? What tool will be used? Why is this technique better for my case? Is my baldness suitable for this method? A transparent clinic will answer clearly."
      }
     },
     {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which technique gives a more natural looking hairline—FUE or DHI?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
       "@type": "Answer",
       "text": "Both can give a natural looking hairline. The naturalness depends more on design and execution than the tool. A natural hairline needs: Correct height Soft irregularity Single-hair grafts in front Proper angle Correct direction Age-appropriate planning Balanced density Direct implantation can help with precise angle control in selected cases. But an experienced FUE surgeon can also create a very natural hairline using slit creation and forceps placement. The surgeon’s skill matters more than the label."
      }
     },
     {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can FUE and Direct Implantation techniques be combined in a single megasession?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
       "@type": "Answer",
       "text": "Yes, they can be combined. In selected megasessions, we may use implanter pen placement for the frontal hairline. Then we may use traditional FUE placement for larger areas like the mid-scalp. This approach can balance precision and efficiency. But it is not needed for every patient. The decision depends on graft count, baldness grade, donor quality, density goals, and surgical planning. A personalised plan is always better than a fixed package."
      }
     }
    ],
